---
description: Every new or changed UI feature needs a ui_tests.rs case
alwaysApply: true
---

# UI features need headless coverage

If you change **user-visible behavior** in the editor (panels, menus, shortcuts,
dialogs, tree, tabs, terminal, agent chrome, save/close flows, …), you must
extend [`src/app/ui_tests.rs`](src/app/ui_tests.rs) in the **same** change —
not “tests later.”

## Do

- Add or update a `#[gpui_kit::test]` that fails if the new behavior regresses.
- Drive the real `IsengardApp` via the existing `Harness` (temp dir, keystrokes /
  `with_app` helpers). Prefer calling app methods when Kit focus/ids are awkward;
  still assert disk/session/panel state.
- Follow patterns already in `ui_tests.rs` and the **UI tests** bullet in
  [docs/architecture.md](docs/architecture.md) (no real agent, no user config,
  no blocking `recv` in `background_spawn`).
- Run the new test (`cargo test <name>`) before finishing.

## Do not

- Ship a UI feature with only unit tests of helpers and no app-level case.
- Skip coverage because “it’s hard to click” — exercise the same code path the
  UI uses (`create_file_in`, `rename_path`, `on_toggle_terminal`, …).
- Launch a real ACP agent or write the user’s `config.json` from tests.

## Out of scope

Pure data/protocol helpers with no UI (e.g. `lsp/edits` string patch, registry
resolve) may stay as plain `#[test]`s. If the change also wires a menu, shortcut,
or panel, still add a `ui_tests` case for that wiring.
